{"shortDescription":"The benchmark S\u0026P 500 (SP500) inched up 0.1% at 7,650.50 points on Friday to close the volatile week that saw the Federal Reserve deliver its first interest rate hike in three years, Treasury yields climb above 5%, and oil prices remain above $100 a barrel.The index was down 0.1% for the week.The F…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The benchmark S\u0026P 500 (",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SP500?utm_source=tradingview\u0026utm_medium=referral\u0026feed_item_type=news","linkText":"SP500"}},") inched up 0.1% at 7,650.50 points on Friday to close the volatile week that saw the Federal Reserve deliver its first interest rate hike in three years, Treasury yields climb above 5%, and oil prices remain above $100 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["The index was down 0.1% for the week."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Fed raised its benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points on Wednesday to a range of 3.75%-4%. The 10-year Treasury yield briefly topped 5% during the week, reaching its highest level since 2007. Crude prices also surged this week after damage to Saudi Arabia's East-West pipeline raised concerns about supply disruptions. Prices retreated from highs of $106 as fears of a prolonged disruption eased, but crude remained above $100 a barrel on Friday."]},{"type":"p","children":["This week's Friday also coincided with quadruple witching, which is when stock-index futures, stock-index options, stock options, and single-stock futures expire, which contributes to volatility."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Technology leads sector gains"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Technology was the S\u0026P 500's strongest-performing sector for the week, with the Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLK","text":"AMEX:XLK"}}," gaining 3.69%. The advance was driven largely by a rebound in semiconductor and chip-equipment stocks. On Friday, Broadcom ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:AVGO","text":"NASDAQ:AVGO"}},", up 3%, and Lam Research ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:LRCX","text":"NASDAQ:LRCX"}}," and Applied Materials ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:AMAT","text":"NASDAQ:AMAT"}},", up about 7%, were among the notable gainers."]},{"type":"p","children":["The technology sector had started the week under pressure after an AI-related selloff, but chip stocks recovered later in the week."]},{"type":"p","children":["Other S\u0026P 500 sectors were mostly lower. Communication Services ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLC","text":"AMEX:XLC"}}," fell 2.5%, Financials ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLF","text":"AMEX:XLF"}}," dropped 2.63%, Utilities ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLU","text":"AMEX:XLU"}}," lost 2.95%, Consumer Staples ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLP","text":"AMEX:XLP"}}," declined 1.77%, Consumer Discretionary ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLY","text":"AMEX:XLY"}}," slipped 1.17%, Materials ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLB","text":"AMEX:XLB"}}," fell 1.40%, Real Estate ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLRE","text":"AMEX:XLRE"}}," dropped 2%, and Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLE","text":"AMEX:XLE"}}," declined 2.44%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Industrials ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLI","text":"AMEX:XLI"}}," gained 0.62%, and Health Care ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"AMEX:XLV","text":"AMEX:XLV"}}," rose 0.30%.",{"type":"disclaimer","children":["Content provided by Seeking Alpha is intended for information purposes only, and that Seeking Alpha does not offer any personalist investment advice and is not a licensed securities dealer, broker, US investment adviser or investment bank."]}]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Economy","args":[{"id":"category","value":"economic"}]},{"title":"Futures","args":[{"